<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saraswati</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sarasvati</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saraswati is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> goddess of knowledge, learning, music and the arts, also identified in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a> with a sacred river. She is usually shown dressed in white, seated on a lotus or accompanied by a swan and playing the veena. Worshipped by students, scholars and musicians, she is also revered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jainism</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, and her festival of Vasant Panchami is celebrated across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saraswati.jpg" alt="Saraswati" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raja Ravi Varma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saraswati.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
